 @eazen  I think it is pretty disingenuous to say that naming doesn’t matter at all. Especially when you say that we can’t jump a naming tier as it “makes no sense”. Can you imagine if in the next generation Intel released an i5 that was quad core? 

What I’m getting at with that is we know the relationship between name and specs means something. It evokes a response based on past naming conventions and if the marketing department doesn’t properly manage those expectations, they’ve done their jobs poorly. 

We may just have to agree to disagree at some point here.

